  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }(\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3x+1))=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3x+1):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/e441953c2cefc6f817a64cb7ce0ebce53164ebb4d3974ae871b14d57450b5167.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3x+1)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3x+1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }(\\pi -\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(3x+1))=\\pi -(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$",
